INT. CALL CENTER - BREAK ROOM - DAY

Beige walls. A microwave with a sticky note: YOU ARE NOT A CHEF. A motivational poster of a rowing team. A vending machine blinking "EXACT CHANGE."

HUGH BANTING, 40s, team lead, polo tucked into khakis, stands at the whiteboard with a marker. YOLANDA PEREIRA, 30s, top agent, headset around her neck, eats yogurt in the corner. GARRETT NG, 20s, the newest, sits at the table with his laptop closed and his hands folded.

HUGH
Team, quick huddle. Great numbers this week.

YOLANDA
Thanks, Hugh.

HUGH
Garrett, I'm proud of you.

GARRETT
Thanks. Hugh.

HUGH
Yolanda, you're a rock star.

YOLANDA
I'm eating.

Hugh caps the marker, uncaps it, and writes SYNERGY on the board, underlines it twice, and steps back like a man admiring a mural. Yolanda scrapes the yogurt cup and drops it in the bin, Garrett checks his phone under the table, and Hugh turns and claps his hands together once, loud as a starter pistol.

HUGH (CONT'D)
Next quarter, we are going bigger.

YOLANDA
How much bigger?

HUGH
Much.

GARRETT
Does that include raises?

HUGH
It includes vision.

YOLANDA
Hugh, honestly, what's the news?

Hugh looks at the whiteboard. At his own handwriting. He sighs, and for the first time the cheerful voice drops out of him.

HUGH
They're closing the floor.

Silence. The vending machine blinks.

GARRETT
Closing it how?

HUGH
Outsourcing. Thirty days.

YOLANDA
Thirty days?

HUGH
I was told not to say.

YOLANDA
You just said.

HUGH
I know.

He wipes the whiteboard with his sleeve, the word SYNERGY smearing to a grey cloud. Yolanda sets her headset on the table. Garrett closes his phone.

GARRETT
(quietly)
Well. Great numbers this week.
